  compression_standard: "
    reference:  core_boot_primer.vsm  — THE density model. Every produced doc
                must read like it: body = notation, prose = // comments.
    degree:     target FORM, not a %: all narrative prose (paragraphs,
                multi-line sentences inside strings) compressed to either
                (a) formal notation — glyphs ⊆ primer.notation ∪ notation_local,
                (b) a single-line // comment giving the rationale, not the story.
                NO EMOJIS (rule 2026-08-06, rmw3): emojis Unicode (ranges
                U+1F000–U+1FAFF, U+2600–U+27BF, U+2B00–U+2BFF, U+1F1E6–U+1F1FF,
                U+FE00–U+FE0F, U+2300–U+23FF) renderizan como caracteres rotos y
                rompen la máquina-lectibilidad. Permitidos SOLO: notación
                matemática VSL (→ ↑ ↓ ↔ ⟺ ⟹ ← ↛) + marcadores de confianza
                ✓ ◐ ◯ ✗ ? (BRIEFING verification markers). Conversión de emoji
                pre-existente: done → ✓ | texto · pending → texto · locked → texto
                · cross → ✗ · warn → ? | texto.
                Empirical deltas (measured 2026-08-06, same rigor each pass):
                comms 746→503 words (−33%, prose-heavy); hard_rules 313→277
                (−11.5%, already dense); regulation_layer 206→194 (−5.8%,
                already dense); instance 121→94 (−22.3%, mixed). A doc already
                in notation compresses little — correct, NOT a failure.
    method:    [1] inventory: list every semantic fact of the source (token
                   inventory, incl. block/field names).
               [2] rewrite each fact: notation if expressible, else // one-liner.
               [3] drop redundant words (the/this/that/will/must) — the field
                   name already carries context.
               [4] merge fields when context covers them.
               [5] bump PROTOCOL_VERSION (per-doc, starts at 1) + header date.
                [6] verify (R4 — never self-report):
                    parser VALID · closure 50 glyphs (verify_primer_closure.py)
                    · token-diff old→new: every semantic token of v1 present
                    in v2 (wording variants allowed, facts not). A missing
                    token = a fact lost — fix, never accept.
                [7] density gate: python3 scripts/vsl/symbol_table.py --density
                    → prose ≤ 5% · words/line ≤ 5.0 (boot/ = 0% · 4.2); over
                    target = not closed (reflow or split, never drop facts).
                [8] paths gate: python3 scripts/vsl/symbol_table.py --paths →
                    system bodies carry @var only (R_ref_resolution); a
                    concrete path in a system body = open item, fix by
                    binding in instance.vsm (instance/ keeps concrete paths).
    exclusions: data values are NOT prose — paths, hostnames, ports, numbers
                (bindings, dim(R), thresholds) stay verbatim. instance/ docs
                keep concrete paths by design (transversal check).",

  // ── TRANSVERSAL CHECKS — applied to every created/moved doc ──
  transversal: [
    "parser: python3 scripts/vsl_parser.py <target> → VALID",
    "NO EMOJIS: scan corpus system/ — emojis Unicode (U+1F000–U+1FAFF, U+2600–U+27BF,
     U+2B00–U+2BFF, U+1F1E6–U+1F1FF, U+FE00–U+FE0F, U+2300–U+23FF) prohibidos; solo
     notación VSL + markers ✓◐◯✗? (regla 2026-08-06 rmw3, ver compression_standard)",
    "DENSITY: python3 scripts/vsl/symbol_table.py --density → prose ≤ 5% ·
     words/line ≤ 5.0 (boot/ = 0% · 4.2); s4-intelligence closed 2026-08-08:
     0% · 4.98 / 3% · 4.15",
    "PATHS: python3 scripts/vsl/symbol_table.py --paths → system bodies @var
     only (R_ref_resolution); bind in instance.vsm, never inline a path",
    "UNIVERSAL docs (boot/meta/theory/ramas) + instance_template/: path line
     root-agnostic // */<dir>/<file> — publication-safe, no instance-bound path
     (ships to GitHub)",
    "INSTANCE config docs (instance/): concrete paths allowed — instance-bound by design",
    "index.md regenerated automatically by pre-commit hook",
    "fuse docs carry gate: claude_review — architecture decision, DS drafts, Claude ratifies",
    "every phase ends with a session() block + commit (session close protocol)",
  ],

  // ── FINAL VERIFICATION (after PH-12) ──
  final: [
    "re-run census against system/ → every doc structured @vsm 1.0",
    "manifest updated → primer deps resolve within boot/",
    "git log clean on feat/ds-s1",
    "ratification: rmw3 approves canonical structure → docs/ → system/ switch",
  ],

    // ── PH-13 — RESTRUCTURE system/ BY DEPENDENCY. rmw3 2026-08-09, AFTER
    //    this plan closes. RECORDED, ¬scheduled: it has a hard prerequisite.
    post: {
      proposal: "rmw3: make the DIRECTORY TREE correspond to the dependency
              graph — every dependency ABOVE its dependents, branches toward
              the trunk. Fuse, move or nest documents so the order serves both
              the graph and the indexing.",

      why_it_is_right: "the tree today is ¬one taxonomy, it is THREE
              overlapping ones:
                S-function   s1-operations … s5-policy            (6)
                role/layer   boot ▪ instance ▪ instance_template ▪ infra (4)
                genre        theory ▪ spec ▪ plan                 (3)
              Three organising principles in one namespace, so ∄ question is
              answerable from a path alone. ONE order derived from MEASUREMENT
              replaces three chosen by habit.
              And a topological tree makes DIRECTORY ORDER = READING ORDER:
              premises before conclusions. That is the boot primer's purpose,
              generalised from six documents to the whole corpus."

      possible_only_now: "until 2026-08-09 the S-function HAD to live in the
              path, because ∄ other place carried it. structure(V) now
              declares the subsystem INSIDE the document, which frees the path
              to encode something else. The proposal is affordable BECAUSE of
              what was ratified today, ¬independently of it."

      hard_prerequisite: "BUILD THE DEPENDENCY GRAPH FIRST. It does not exist —
              cycle task 3, never started. Restructuring before measuring is
              reordering by intuition, which is the exact defect this cycle
              corrected four times over: the grammar gate, the pydantic
              differential, the BASIN_FLOOR classification, the axiom debt.
              Every label was a HYPOTHESIS, ¬a specification."

      known_limit: "dependencies form a DAG, ¬a tree. boot/vsl_language is
              depended on by nearly everything and can live in ONE directory.
              The tree can encode DEPTH (trunk → branches) and ¬the whole
              graph. The GRAPH stays canonical; the tree is a PROJECTION of
              it. Treating the tree AS the graph would be a second source of
              truth."

      cost: "moving a file breaks every @ref, every binding, every
              spec_kernel_reconcile citation — and §recertification is
              explicit: a MECHANICAL edit DECERTIFIES a document until the
              touched sites are re-read. 48 documents. So it happens ONCE,
              driven by the measured graph, with the re-read budgeted INSIDE
              the move ¬as a follow-up."
      // debt(SYSTEM-TREE-BY-DEPENDENCY, class=doc, owner=rmw3, gate=dep_graph_built)
      // Sequence: dependency graph → tree proposal → ONE move + re-read pass.
    },

  // ── RECONCILE 2026-08-15 (rmw3 directive — plan as LIVE TREE) ──
  // PH-09/10/11 declared targets under system/ that do NOT live there:
  //   PH-09 infra/      → system/instance/infra/infra_ops.vsm (instance-bound)
  //   PH-10 plan/       → docs/plans/* (plans_active, revision_arc_tree)
  //   PH-11 spec/       → plan/vsf-vsl-revision/phase-spec/ (los 4 experimentos
  //                       viven DENTRO del plan — PART III, no spec/ raíz)
  // The PHASE TABLE above remains the phase SOURCE; the live-state
  // PROJECTION is plan/revision-arc-tree/revision_arc_tree.vsm (derived, checks/plan-tree-valid).
  // PH-00..PH-08 + PH-12 are structurally COMPLETE (docs present); only
  // ratification (@status) of kernel/s5-policy/s4/s3/s2/s1 remains.
  reconcile_2026_08_15: {
    status: done,
    what: "targets corregidos al lugar real; fases mapeadas; árbol derivado
           creado (revision_arc_tree.vsm, 58% del arco completado); bloque
           STRATEGIC envuelto en plans_active.vsm; gate plan-tree-valid en
           pre-commit (drift → bloquea)."
  },
}

